:null,"_gp_spread":null,"_score_spread":null,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":null,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":null,"_gp_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":null,"_gate_pool_share":null,"_gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.023539750792504942,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":37.3,"_gate_share_shrink":null,"_gp_share_shrink":null,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.013966937799322851,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":76.7,"_gate_insider_own":0.15049,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":100.0,"_gate_insider_buying":0.538,"_gp_insider_buying":true,"_score_insider_buying":53.8,"pf":[],"description_full":"Burke & Herbert Financial Services Corp. operates as the bank holding company for Burke & Herbert Bank & Trust Company that provides various community banking products and services in the United States. The company offers consumer and commercial deposit products, such as digital banking, demand, negotiable order of withdrawal, money market, and savings accounts; and certificates of deposit. It also provides loans comprising commercial real estate, single family residential, owner-occupied commercial real estate, commercial and industrial, residential mortgage, and consumer non-real estate and other loans, as well as acquisition, construction, and development loans. In addition, it offers cash management services; online and mobile banking; and wealth and trust services. Further, the company provides business solutions, including small business and commercial checking and savings options; investment services; and treasury management solutions consist of a suite of digital banking, payables, receivables, and risk management, as well as automated cash flow comprising enhanced reporting, automated clearing house, wires, remote deposit capture, bill pay, lockbox, credit and debit cards, merchant services, fraud protection, and deposit and loan sweeps. Burke & Herbert Financial Services Corp. was founded in 1852 and is headquartered in Alexandria, Virginia.","ceo_bio":"Mr. David P. Boyle CPA | Chair & CEO | Age 61 | Compensation: $2.2M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $332K ranks in the bottom quartile among Financial Services peers, with revenue growing 75%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $93K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $5K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 7\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (6/10).","financial_summary":["Burke & Herbert Financial Servi is a small-cap financial services business with a $1.4B market cap on $342M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +75% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder. Operating margins are expanding by +10.0pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at 7% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $96M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 28 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, with adequate 0.92\u00d7 cash conversion.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA.","Shareholder yield of 2.4% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 15% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and within its sector the business captures 1.6\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.3) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 13% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Trading at a 49% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","19 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Growing faster than most Financial Services peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Understanding Momentum Shifts in (BHRB)","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/101/Understanding_Momentum_Shifts_in_BHRB_111026033002_1794299402.html","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794299402.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Comparing Burke & Herbert Financial Services (NASDAQ:BHRB) & BV Financial (NASDAQ:BVFL)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/07/comparing-burke-bv-financial-nasdaqbvfl.html","date":"2026-11-07","timestamp":1794094128.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.909,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Burke & Herbert Financial Services (BHRB) Could Be 1% Below Fair Value After Mixed Earnings","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/banks/nasdaq-bhrb/burke-herbert-financial-services/news/burke-herbert-financial-services-bhrb-could-be-1-below-fair","date":"2026-11-02","timestamp":1793640340.487,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.878,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Contrasting Burke & Herbert Financial Services (NASDAQ:BHRB) and NB Bancorp (NASDAQ:NBBK)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/10/31/contrasting-burke-herbert-financial-services-nasdaqbhrb-and-nb-bancorp-nasdaqnbbk.html","date":"2026-10-31","timestamp":1793441708.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.909,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"How (BHRB) Movements Inform Risk Allocation Models","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/91/How_BHRB_Movements_Inform_Risk_Allocation_Models_103126042202_1793434922.html","date":"2026-10-31","timestamp":1793434922.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.494,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Burke & Herbert Financial Services Re